So you installed a snapshot and then compiled a -release kernel if i got
that right. Now you got a -release kernel running on a -current userland
which is not really recommended and most likely is the cause for your
login problems.
I would suggest booting into single user and do a cp /bsd.old /bsd, then
reboot with this original snapshot kernel.
If that works and login is possible disable de(4) with config(8)
(config -e -o /bsd /bsd).
Afterwards, your alpha should be back in business.

Regards,
Martin

